from printkit.common import ROOT, render_html, merge_pdfs

def build():
    from pathlib import Path
    import html
    d=ROOT / "Art/Station_1"
    css="""@page{size:letter;margin:.5in}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#ddd;color:#25152e;font-family:Georgia,serif}.page{width:7.5in;height:9.95in;background:white;margin:20px auto;break-after:page;overflow:hidden}h1{font-size:23px;margin:0 0 12px}h2{font-size:17px;margin:12px 0 6px}p,li{font-size:13px;line-height:1.4}.row{display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:.15in;flex-wrap:wrap}.cut{border:1px dashed #aaa}.statue{display:block;width:4in;height:6in;object-fit:contain;margin:.1in auto}.sheet{width:7.35in;height:4.9in;object-fit:contain;display:block;margin:auto}.clue{width:7.2in;height:4.8in;object-fit:contain;display:block;margin:auto}.plate{width:5in;height:3in;object-fit:contain;display:block;margin:auto}.crest{width:3in;height:3in;object-fit:contain}.standee{width:1.34in;height:2in;object-fit:contain}.gargoyle{width:2in;height:3in;object-fit:contain}.slips{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3.5in 3.5in;gap:.15in;justify-content:center}.slip{width:3.5in;height:2in;padding:.13in;border:3px double #92703a;background:#eee3d4;font-size:14pt;line-height:1.22}.slip strong{display:block;font-size:14pt;margin-bottom:5px}.title{border:1px dashed #999;padding:10px;width:3.5in;font-size:15px}.screen{padding:15px;max-width:900px;margin:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font:12px/1.3 Arial}th,td{border:1px solid #aaa;padding:7px;text-align:left}th{background:#eee}@media print{body{background:white}.screen{display:none}.page{margin:0}}"""
    def page(t,b):return '<section class="page"><h1>'+t+'</h1>'+b+'</section>'
    def doc(t,b):return '<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>'+t+'</title><style>'+css+'</style></head><body><div class="screen"><button onclick="print()">Print</button> Letter • 100% scale • background graphics ON • browser headers/footers OFF.</div>'+b+'</body></html>'
    names=['Victoria','Alexi','Teresa','Valerius','Borislav','Barov']
    player=''
    for n in names:
     player+=page('The Library — Ancestor Statue',f'<img class="statue cut" src="statue_{n.lower()}.png"><p>Cut out the 4 × 6 inch card. Place flat or use a card holder.</p>')
    player+=page('The Six Stone Relics','<img class="sheet cut" src="stone_relic_tokens.png"><p>Cut the six tokens apart along the white gutters. Each is approximately 2.4 inches square. Lay them on the reading table; place a chosen token beside a statue when making an offering.</p><h2>The Watcher</h2><img class="gargoyle cut" src="gargoyle_watcher.png"><p>Cut along the white silhouette. Mount in a clip or fold the base tab onto a card foot.</p>')
    (d/'Station_1_Player_Print_Pack.html').write_text(doc('Station 1 — player starting props',player))
    details=['Black ink is ground into her fingertips and thumbs.','Dried, flaking mud is caked on his boots and coat hem.','Dark crimson stains her palms and the skin under her fingernails.','He smells of salt and brine. Tiny barnacles cling to his shoulder plates.','Black soot smears his jaw, knuckles and forearms.','Nothing. No stain, no grime, not even dust. He gleams as if polished this morning.']
    reveals=page('DM-held inspection slips','<p>Cut apart before play. Give only the slip earned by inspecting that statue; keep all others hidden.</p><div class="slips">'+''.join(f'<div class="slip"><strong>{i+1} — {n}</strong>{html.escape(t)}</div>' for i,(n,t) in enumerate(zip(names,details)))+'</div>')
    reveals+=page('DM-held progressive clues','<p>Reading table: reveal at minute 2–3 if needed, or when the runner is lifted. Cut the art apart from these instructions.</p><img class="clue cut" src="reading_table_inscription.png"><p>Plinth plate: reveal at minute 8–9, automatically by 9:00.</p><img class="plate cut" src="plinth_plate.png">')
    titles=['Arch-Librarian Victoria','Lord Alexi the Harvester','Lady Teresa the Traitor','Admiral Valerius','Forge-Master Borislav','King Barov the Spotless']
    reveals+=page('DM-held reward and encounter','<div class="row"><div><h2>Archive Crest #1</h2><img class="crest cut" src="archive_crest_token.png"></div><div><h2>Spectre</h2><img class="standee cut" src="spectre_standee.png"></div></div><p>Give the crest only when all six relics are matched. Reveal the Spectre only after the crown/dagger taboo swap. Cut its silhouette and mount in a clip or on a folded base.</p><h2>Full-title labels — reveal after success</h2><div class="row">'+''.join('<div class="title">'+html.escape(t)+'</div>' for t in titles)+'</div><p>Keep these separate until solved. Do not print titles on the backs of player cards where they might be seen early.</p>')
    (d/'Station_1_Reveals_Print_Pack.html').write_text(doc('Station 1 — DM-held slips and reveals',reveals))
    items=['Book','Scythe','Dagger','Spear','Hammer','Crown']
    dm=page('DM ONLY — Library answer & running sheet','<table><tr><th>Statue</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Relic</th></tr>'+''.join(f'<tr><td>{i+1} {n}</td><td>{html.escape(t)}</td><td>{x}</td></tr>' for i,(n,t,x) in enumerate(zip(names,details,items)))+'</table><h2>Setup & inspection</h2><p>Place six statues and relic tokens; raise Barov on a small box or book. Put the gargoyle above the table. Hide slips, inscriptions, full titles, Spectre and crest.</p><p>Investigation DC 13: Fred +4, Griffin +5. Success earns the detail slip. Failure invites a new approach next turn; never lock out the clue. Barov needs no roll on a close inspection (Mage Hand, climb, or close study after Clue 3).</p><h2>Character hooks</h2><p>Fred: once this station, Let’s Split Up gives both partners advantage inspecting different statues. Griffin: invisible, so immune to the gargoyle’s sight-based shriek; Mage Hand reaches Barov without a climb. Otherwise climb Athletics DC 12.</p><h2>Misplacements</h2><p>Every wrong placement drops ALL placed relics back to the table. On the second and later wrong placements, gargoyle shrieks: DC 12 Wisdom or 1d6 psychic to visible characters. Griffin is never targeted.</p><p><b>Taboo swap:</b> dagger to Barov or crown to Teresa releases Spectre: AC 12, HP 14, +4 to hit, 1d6 necrotic. Warn neutrally before every crown or dagger placement, whether the proposed match is right or wrong. Handling and inspection are safe. An offering to a statue counts as placement; moving a token around the table does not.</p>')
    dm+=page('DM ONLY — Coaching & emergency clues','<h2>Opening</h2><p>Six stone ancestors wait with empty hands. Six relics lie under a rumpled velvet runner. A stone gargoyle watches. Barov stands on a taller plinth. Do not name professions or announce stains before inspection.</p><h2>2–3 minutes</h2><p>“That velvet runner is lumpy. Anyone curious?” Lifting the runner reveals the reading-table inscription; by 3:00 let it slide away if they need help.</p><h2>5–6 minutes</h2><p>“Your sheet says you love splitting up. Anything there that fits?” For Griffin: “Barov’s hands are way up there. Anything that reaches?” Give the earned detail slips, not the item answers.</p><h2>8–9 minutes</h2><p>Reveal the plinth plate. “Look closely at what isn’t there.” If they have not found it by 9:00, the plate cracks free automatically.</p><h2>Emergency — only after taboo swap or stuck at 11:00</h2><p>The ghost librarian whispers: “Give the book to the ink, the scythe to the mud, the hammer to the soot, the spear to the brine, the crown to the spotless one, and the dagger to the blood!”</p><p>At 11:00 say only the pairs still missing. At 13:00 give the full line if needed. Open the gate by 15:00.</p><h2>Protect deduction</h2><p>Do not confirm guesses until a token is placed. Reward creative inspection. Keep the same warning for correct and incorrect crown/dagger choices. Cap unrelated combat or semantic debates at about a minute, then redirect toward evidence.</p><p><b>Source:</b> Stations/Station_1_Library_Crown_and_Dagger.md. The placement-trigger rule above follows the explicit Failure Consequences section.</p>')
    (d/'Station_1_DM_Notes.html').write_text(doc('Station 1 — DM only',dm))
    print('Created 7 player pages, 3 reveal pages, 2 DM pages.')
